# ReWorth — stack rules

| Area | Decision |
| --- | --- |
| Monorepo | Turborepo + pnpm |
| **Primary client** | **React Native + Expo** (`apps/mobile`) — iOS + Android |
| Web companion | Next.js 15 App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind (`apps/web`) — browse / search / PDP / checkout |
| Admin | Next.js 15 (`apps/admin`) — ops only; not a consumer surface |
| API | NestJS modular monolith, REST `/api/v1` |
| DB | PostgreSQL 16 + Prisma; Redis + BullMQ |
| Media | S3-compatible object store (`STORAGE_DRIVER=s3`, `S3StorageAdapter`); local compose runs **adobe/s3mock**; disk fallback (`STORAGE_DRIVER=local`) |
| Search | OpenSearch + Postgres FTS fallback |
| Auth | JWT + email/password + Google/Apple OAuth |
| Push | Mock default; `PUSH_PROVIDER=expo` for store |
| Payments | Paystack + mock PSP; escrow-shaped (ADR-002) |
| AI | OpenAI GPT-4o default + rule-based mock |
| Locale | NGN, en-NG, WAT |

## Surface priority

1. Mobile (iOS + Android)  
2. Web companion parity  
3. Admin (ops)

Stack changes require a new ADR under `docs/ADRS/`. See ADR-001.
